        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newfane%2C_Vermont"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Governor Benning Wentworth originally named the town Fane after an English nobleman before renaming it Newfane in 1761.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        10,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newfane%2C_Vermont"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Newfane Village is listed on the National Register of Historic Places and is one of the most photographed villages in Vermont.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.historicalsocietyofwindhamcounty.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The County History Museum in Newfane is located inside the historic 1825 county jail building.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.historicalsocietyofwindhamcounty.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The West River Railroad Museum in Newfane is housed in the original railroad station and water tank house built in 1880.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12
